From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:45:55 +0100
Subject: GUI: no second comparison while one is still running

Since b041592 ("render a pair only when its words match") the workers
read MainWindow's fingerprint cache while comparePagesInParallel() runs,
and while it runs the progress callback processes events.  Nothing that
changes the cache may run then, but a second comparison could start:

  1. Click Cancel.  compare() set the button back to "Compare" at once,
     though the workers were still finishing their current pairs.
  2. Click Compare, step a page, or change the page offset.  These
     checked whether the button read "&Cancel", which it no longer did,
     so a second runComparison() started inside the first.
  3. That reset cancel to false, so the first comparison's workers went
     on taking pairs, reading the cache while the second comparison
     erased and inserted entries in it, on the main thread.

Before b041592 this gave odd results but no data race, since only the
main thread touched the cache.

Keep a comparing flag, set from the start of a comparison until
comparePages() returns, and check it instead of the button's text.
Cancel now only sets cancel and disables the button, which becomes
"Compare" again once the workers have stopped.

Also bring comparePagesInParallel()'s comment up to date: the workers
take pairs, not pages, so a page in several pairs may be read once for
each; progress counts pairs; and the cache must not change while it runs.

